{% doc %}
  Shared body of the two SendGrid Inbound Parse endpoints.

  @param email [String] the raw MIME message, SendGrid's `email` field
  @param envelope [String] SendGrid's `envelope` field, JSON
  @param token [String] the shared secret from the URL
  @return [Object] the result of commands/inbound/receive
{% enddoc %}
{%- comment -%}
  Both pages that use this are thin: they call it, then set the response
  status and echo the JSON. The work lives here so the two routes cannot
  drift apart.

  Two routes exist on purpose. `support/inbound/sendgrid` is the original
  and the one the current Parse host points at. `api/support/inbound/sendgrid`
  matches the path used by the only host on this SendGrid account that
  delivers, so a second Parse host can be pointed at it with nothing else
  different. Keep both until the inbound delivery problem is settled.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  comment
    Every arrival is logged before the secret is checked, and that is the
    point of it: a refused post writes nothing anywhere else, so without
    this line "the provider never called us" and "the provider called us
    and we said no" look identical from the outside. Inbound Parse keeps
    no log of its own at the provider, so this is the only record that an
    email reached the door.

    The delivery envelope only: who sent it and where it was addressed,
    both small and both already known to the provider. Not the token,
    which would put the endpoint's whole authentication in the log, and
    not the message, which is the customer's.
  endcomment
  log envelope, type: 'modules/support/inbound: a post arrived'

  comment
    The pages read `context.params` one named key at a time and pass the
    values in. Never the hash itself: in the provider's parsed mode a
    posted file arrives as a Rails object with no Liquid representation,
    and touching the hash as a whole, passing it on included, raises
    before anything can run.
  endcomment
  function neutral = 'modules/support/helpers/email/from_raw', raw: email, envelope: envelope, token: token
  function result = 'modules/support/commands/inbound/receive', params: neutral
  return result
-%}
